	<key>readme</key>
	<string>Two independent flat keywords, no chaining. ghr: main worktrees only (.git is a directory), one repo-link entry each, no network calls. ghp: every dir under ~/src/factify with a .git, one gh pr view per dir in parallel, one item per open PR. Both feed the same Open URL (default) and clipboard (cmd) actions. A chained Script-Filter-to-Script-Filter design was tried first (pick a project, then fetch just its PRs) but Alfred invokes the downstream filter with a null argument on arrival (confirmed via the workflow debugger: "Queuing argument '(null)'") even though the bar shows the picked item's text — the visible query and the actual script argv are not the same thing for that connection type. Not worth fighting; flat list it is.</string>
